<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=tractor">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Farming and food</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tractor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1889">1889</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A tractor is an engine-powered vehicle that pulls or drives farm machinery. The first tractors were steam ploughing engines, which followed the self-propelled traction engine Thomas Aveling made in 1859; in 1889 John Charter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a> built the first gasoline-powered tractors, and John Froelich built another in Iowa in 1892. Dan Albone's Ivel Agricultural Motor of 1901 was the first commercially successful light petrol tractor, and Henry Ford's mass-produced Fordson of 1917 held 77% of the US market by 1923. By 1935 nearly a million tractors were in use in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tractor.jpg" alt="Tractor" width="330" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mulad · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ford_8N.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…the &quot;Red Letter&quot; of the party's Central Committee and a peasant woman holding a sheaf of rice; the horse has named trucks, buses and <b>tractors</b>, a line of the Pyongyang Metro, the national football team and a rocket, and has appeared on banknotes since 1978 and on stamps.</blockquote><a href="/songs/chollima-on-the-wing">Chollima on the Wing</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1889</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Illinois, United States</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>John Charter · John Froelich · Dan Albone</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Steam came first: Thomas Aveling made a portable engine self-propelled in 1859, and steam ploughing engines, used in pairs to haul a plough by cable, were the first tractors.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/steam-engine">Steam engine<span>1606</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/internal-combustion-engine">Internal combustion engine<span>1794</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=tractor">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
